# Critical Findings & Cross-Cutting Themes

## 1. ACCESSIBILITY & INCLUSION (Dimension 5) — STILL WEAKEST ACROSS ALL 20 AREAS

No area rated itself as having robust WCAG 2.2 AA practice, systematic AT offer, or proactive accessibility culture. Most areas: "Accessibility mentioned but not systematic." HBH/EYE & some others note this as gap.

Action: College-wide Accessibility Teach-Meet (Week 2–3) remains URGENT. All 20 areas should attend. Focus: Accessibility Checker, WCAG basics, Immersive Reader, Live Captions, UDL assignment design.

## 2. DIGITAL LEAD CONFIRMATION & CLARITY

PRE EMPLOYMENT (Laura Taylor): DL marked as "?" — Urgent clarification needed by EOW.

MATHS (Jason Clear): DL selection unclear — "Denholm Wilcox, Diego Fanhe & Joel Baylis were put forward - but we have not heard who selected." Decision needed ASAP.

BUS (Ben Melhuish): DL listed as "TBC - sorry!" — Needs confirmation (Ben himself or named colleague?).

All other 17 areas: DLs clearly named ✓

## 3. INFRASTRUCTURE GAPS (INFRASTRUCTURE-DEPENDENT AREAS)

Network/WiFi: CON/BUI/MOT (workshop areas), CREATIVE_DIGITAL, EEY (corridor).

Software licensing: CRM (BUS), CAD (CON/MOT), Diagnostics (MOT), CS apps (SIX), Cloud platforms (all).

Hardware: Devices in most areas adequate; Pre Employment & some support services may need assessment.

Action: IT infrastructure audit Week 1. Software licensing conversation with Joe A (procurement pathway & budget).

## 4. COLLEGE-WIDE QUICK WINS (BY WEEK 4)

100% Century Initial Assessment completion (all 20 areas)

One specialist digital skills rubric per area (domain-specific)

All 9 DLs trained on Health Check framework

Accessibility Teach-Meet completed (all 20 areas attend)

